import ../../../testing/driver.dl
import lib/text_scan.dl

appearance range page appearance:
    maximum width is 440
    padding is 12
    gap is 12

appearance range field appearance:
    padding is 10
    minimum height is 52
    background is UI ink 245 247 249
    text is UI ink 22 28 36
    accent is UI ink 65 100 210
    border is UI ink 170 180 190
    border width is 1
    corner radius is 6

document range controls using range page appearance:
    range field "Progress" from 0.0 through 100.0 stepping 0.5 initially 25.0 using range field appearance
    range field "Trim" from -2.0 through 2.0 stepping 0.25 initially -0.75 using range field appearance
    range field "Fixed" from 2.0 through 2.0 stepping 0.5 initially 2.0 using range field appearance
    code:
        when the "Progress" control changes:
            notice test range this window

window range desktop:
    group at 0 0 sized 400 by 180:
        range field "Desktop frame" from 0.0 through 1.0 stepping 0.01 initially 0.25 using range field appearance

# Programmatic updates and user changes have separate effects.
to notice test range {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    set changes to instance's state as a pointer to an integer
    set the value at changes to (the value at changes) + 1

to press range test key {integer:key} in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    queue UI input of kind 3 key key at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in view
    ignore update UI view view

set changes to 0
set instance to an instance of range controls with state (the address of changes)
set window to the address of instance
set other to an instance of range controls
require condition ((the range value of "Progress" in window) = 25.0) reporting "A range lost its declared initial value."
require condition ((the range value of "Trim" in window) = -0.75) reporting "A range lost its negative fractional bounds."
set the range value of "Progress" in window to 18.4
require condition ((the range value of "Progress" in window) = 18.5) reporting "A range did not snap to its authored step."
require condition ((the range value of "Progress" in (the address of other)) = 25.0) reporting "Two instances shared a range value."
set revision to window's revision
set the range value of "Progress" in window to 18.5
require condition (window's revision = revision) reporting "Assigning the same range value invalidated the UI."
set the range value of "Progress" in window to -5.0
require condition ((the range value of "Progress" in window) = 0.0) reporting "A range accepted a value below its minimum."
set the range value of "Progress" in window to 150.0
require condition ((the range value of "Progress" in window) = 100.0) reporting "A range accepted a value above its maximum."
set the range value of "Progress" in window to 25.0
require condition (changes = 0) reporting "Programmatic range updates invoked an input callback."

set view to a UI view of window sized 600 by 500 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
set progress to the UI layout labeled "Progress" in (view's layout)
require condition ((progress's bounds' width > 100.0) and (progress's bounds' height >= 52.0)) reporting "A range did not reserve its authored layout."
require condition (progress's appearance's accent's blue = 210) reporting "A range ignored its authored accent color."
require condition ((view's window as a pointer to test UI surface)'s drawn contains "Progress") reporting "A range did not paint its caption."
set middle to progress's painted bounds' y + progress's bounds' height / 2.0
set center to progress's painted bounds' x + progress's bounds' width / 2.0
queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at center middle with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 1 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((the range value of "Progress" in window) = 50.0) reporting "Clicking the middle of a range did not choose its midpoint."
queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at (progress's painted bounds' x - 100.0) middle with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((the range value of "Progress" in window) = 0.0) reporting "Dragging outside a range lost pointer capture."
queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at (progress's painted bounds' x + progress's bounds' width + 100.0) middle with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 0 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (((the range value of "Progress" in window) = 100.0) and (changes = 3)) reporting "Dragging did not report each changed range value exactly once."

press range test key 258 in (the address of view)
require condition ((view's focused = progress) and view's keyboard focus) reporting "A range was missing from keyboard focus."
press range test key 263 in (the address of view)
require condition ((the range value of "Progress" in window) = 99.5) reporting "A range ignored its keyboard step."
press range test key 267 in (the address of view)
require condition ((the range value of "Progress" in window) = 94.5) reporting "A range ignored its page step."
press range test key 268 in (the address of view)
require condition ((the range value of "Progress" in window) = 0.0) reporting "Home did not reach the range minimum."
press range test key 269 in (the address of view)
require condition (((the range value of "Progress" in window) = 100.0) and (changes = 7)) reporting "End did not reach the range maximum."
set the "Progress" control in window enabled false
queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at center middle with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 1 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 0 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (((the range value of "Progress" in window) = 100.0) and (changes = 7)) reporting "A disabled range accepted pointer input."
set view's width to 300
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (progress's bounds' width <= 300.0) reporting "A range did not follow its resized viewport."
require condition ((the range value of "Fixed" in window) = 2.0) reporting "A zero-span range lost its fixed value."
close the address of view
close window
close the address of other

set desktop to an instance of range desktop
set surface to a UI view of (the address of desktop) sized 600 by 500 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view (the address of surface)
set field to the UI layout labeled "Desktop frame" in (surface's layout)
require condition ((surface's window as a pointer to test UI surface)'s drawn contains "Desktop frame") reporting "A classic window did not paint its range."
set location to field's painted bounds
queue UI input of kind 1 key 0 at (location's x + location's width / 2.0) (location's y + location's height / 2.0) with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of surface)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 1 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of surface)
queue UI input of kind 2 key 0 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of surface)
ignore update UI view (the address of surface)
require condition ((the range value of "Desktop frame" in (the address of desktop)) = 0.5) reporting "A classic window range disagreed with document input."
close the address of surface
close the address of desktop
print line "Ranges share stepped values, pointer capture, keyboard navigation, disabled states and responsive drawing."
